      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The long-term follow-up of acquired coronary artery to left ventricle fistula is unclear. We describe 2 cases of coronary artery to left ventricle fistula monitored for an average of 15 years with no clinical or echocardiographic deterioration. Medical therapy appears to be the appropriate treatment strategy in these patients."},
